 [{:section/type :accuracy-pointer,
   :section/id 17,
   :section/title "Would you all like a coffee?",
   :section/body
   ["Les gustaría un café?"
    "You will remember these structures Le gusta you like Le gustaría you would like A more literal translation could be to you it is pleasing Le gusta to you it would be pleasing Le gustaría Le means to you So to say to you plural (to you all) in Spanish is les Therefore to you all it is pleasing Les gusta to you all it would be pleasing Les gustaría Again I remind you to think of these as complete phrases and use them as complete phrases and you won't go wrong."]}],
 :lesson/number 20,
 :lesson/intro [],
 :lesson/step {:step/number 4, :step/title "They do talk, don’t they?"},
 :lesson/closing
 ["Congratulations you have almost finished step 4 You are almost finish with this part, you have a little more to learn."
  "No more Synergy Verbs."
  "11 more Mortar in step 5 You just need to learn another 3 Brick Verbs and an easy structure to make your Spanish more natural."],
